### Networking and Security Group Rules Tests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8085/api/v1/ec2

### 1. Create a Security Group
# @name createSG
POST {{baseUrl}}/security-groups
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "web-server-sg",
    "description": "Security group for web servers"
}

###

@sgId = {{createSG.response.body.data.id}}

### 2. List Security Groups
GET {{baseUrl}}/security-groups

### 3. Get Security Group Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/security-groups/{{sgId}}

### 4. Add Inbound Rule (TCP 80)
POST {{baseUrl}}/security-groups/{{sgId}}/rules
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "type": "inbound",
    "protocol": "tcp",
    "from_port": 80,
    "to_port": 80,
    "source_dest_cidr": "0.0.0.0/0",
    "description": "Allow HTTP"
}

### 5. Add Inbound Rule (TCP 443)
POST {{baseUrl}}/security-groups/{{sgId}}/rules
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "type": "inbound",
    "protocol": "tcp",
    "from_port": 443,
    "to_port": 443,
    "source_dest_cidr": "0.0.0.0/0",
    "description": "Allow HTTPS"
}

### 6. Add Outbound Rule (Allow All)
POST {{baseUrl}}/security-groups/{{sgId}}/rules
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "type": "outbound",
    "protocol": "all",
    "source_dest_cidr": "0.0.0.0/0",
    "description": "Allow all outbound"
}

### 7. List Instances to get an ID
# @name listInstances
GET {{baseUrl}}/instances

###

@instanceId = {{listInstances.response.body.data[0].id}}

### 8. Assign SG to Instance
POST {{baseUrl}}/instances/{{instanceId}}/security-groups
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "security_group_id": {{sgId}}
}

### 9. List SGs for Instance
GET {{baseUrl}}/instances/{{instanceId}}/security-groups

### 10. Remove Rule (requires actual rule ID from response 4 or 5)
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/security-groups/{{sgId}}/rules/1
